## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | re-introduced | BLOCKING | js/common/tcTriage.js | 🚨 blocking ci red — crap ratchet fails 15 new functions over threshold 8 worst offender is dead code the crap check failed on head 056b9cea ci failures md log line 0 regression s 15 new over threshold 8 improvement s exit code 2 so the merge gate is red the single worst offender is this function samebuildandenv js common tctriage js cc 8 cov 0 0 crap 72 0 samebuildandenv is never called anywhere — not by triagevalidatedguard which uses samebuild envchanged directly not by any caller not by any test grep rn samebuildandenv finds only its definition and export deleting it removes the 72 crap entry entirely the remaining 14 over threshold functions need decomposition before the ratchet passes new functions must land ≤ 8 js poststorytestautomationresults js triagebugfailures 19 5 entryrolemeta 17 1 handlebugwithproductfailure 16 1 currentbuildsha 10 4 js common tcmaintenanceledger js normalizefinding 17 findingfromverdict 16 findingfromdevclaim 11 findingline 11 2 js common tcrunregistry js recordgreen 16 recordfailure 14 js common tctriage js pickevidence 14 resolvetcrole 10 js developbugandcreatepr js completetestsuspectedpath 12 2 js unit tests test poststorytestautomationresults js triagemodule 9 concrete refactor guidance extract per entry step helpers triagebugfailures → one entry function table drive pickevidence normalizefinding field copying with a key sourcekeys loop split recordgreen recordfailure entry construction into a shared mergeentrystate helper and split entryrolemeta source selection into a small resolver chain all are pure functions — the existing 51 new unit tests keep passing through mechanical extraction |
| F11 | open | BLOCKING | js/common/tcRunRegistry.js | 🚨 blocking ci red again on head 2bf29a71 — the crap check now fails the duplication ratchet 3 fresh duplications the complexity half of the previous round is verifiably fixed fresh ci log 0 regression s 0 new over threshold 0 improvement s 0 removed — thank you but the same crap check still exits 2 on the current head now from the gh 1251 duplication ratchet fresh duplication js common findingregistry js 2 38 not pinned in duplication baseline json fresh duplication js common tcmaintenanceledger js 3 16 not pinned in duplication baseline json fresh duplication js common tcrunregistry js 7 29 not pinned in duplication baseline json duplication ratchet fail — 3 fresh 0 regressed 1 pinned debt files unchanged the duplicated block is visible in this diff markersafe markersafereplacer are byte identical across tcrunregistry js 149 tcmaintenanceledger js 313 and the pre existing findingregistry js 662 and each file repeats the same parsexcomments shape reviewverdicts collectallowedrecords atms date parse timestamp comparator sort tcrunregistry js 209 220 tcmaintenanceledger js 371 382 findingregistry js 760 770 findingregistry js is not touched by this pr — the new marker modules similarity dragged it over threshold too — but the two new files are this pr s additions so the red gate is this pr s to clear tcrunregistry js at 7 29 is the worst fix options in order of preference 1 extract the shared marker plumbing into one module e g js common markercomments js markersafe markersafereplacer and a parsemarkercomments comments opts prefix suffix payloadadapter that wraps collectallowedrecords stamps atms and applies the shared comparator each of the three modules keeps only its marker prefix and payload adapter the existing marker round trip tests in all three suites keep passing the adapters are pure 2 if the team prefers the debt route pin all three files in duplication baseline json per the regeneration process documented in that file s note — but deduplicating here is small safe and clears the debt instead of growing it either way the crap check must go green on a new head before merge |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

diff --git a/js/common/reviewVerdicts.js b/js/common/reviewVerdicts.js
index e753415ca..dd7f420c4 100644
--- a/js/common/reviewVerdicts.js
+++ b/js/common/reviewVerdicts.js
@@ -244,6 +244,79 @@ function markerRecordComparator(a, b) {
     return (a.order || 0) - (b.order || 0);
 }

+// ── gh-1329 rework: the shared marker plumbing ───────────────────────────────
+// The three machine-marker modules (findingRegistry, tcRunRegistry,
+// tcMaintenanceLedger) carried byte-identical copies of the marker-hygiene
+// escaping and the parse-records walk — the gh-1251 duplication ratchet
+// flagged all three files (tcRunRegistry 7.29% was the red gate). The shared
+// helpers live here, beside the walk's other halves (collectAllowedRecords,
+// extractMarkerJson, markerRecordComparator); every marker module now
+// delegates.
+
+// Marker-hostile sequences: an embedded `-->` would terminate the HTML
+// comment (visually on GitHub, and for the next round's suffix-search
+// parse), and an embedded `<!--` would shadow the marker prefix search. A
+// zero-width space breaks both sequences while staying invisible in the
+// rendered text.
+function markerSafe(text) {
+    return String(text || '')
+        .replace(/-->/g, '--\u200b>')
+        .replace(/<!--/g, '<!\u200b--');
+}
+
+// Every string entering a marker payload is marker-safe — free text (reviewer
+// text is data, not protocol) can never break out of the marker format.
+function markerSafeReplacer(key, value) {
+    return typeof value === 'string' ? markerSafe(value) : value;
+}
+
+// The configured-identity gate for the FAIL-CLOSED marker families (the run
+// registry and the maintenance ledger re-route bug verdicts, so an absent
+// allowlist trusts nothing). The finding registry keeps its shape-agnostic
